Modification History:

 *** NOTE ***
 DO NOT UPDATE THIS FILE. UPDATE package.xml INSTEAD.
  This file contains the CHANGELOG for the initial release. For subsequent
  releases, the CHANGLELOG is maintained in the package.xml file itself.
  Please edit package.xml instead.
 ************

 Unreleased   security fixes, crash fixes, robustness fixes, test additions
              and behavior changes
              for the next release (release notes move to package.xml).
              - Security: fix XSS via URL parameters and report data; fix path
                traversal and PHP object injection via unserialize in custom
                run id handling.
              - Crash fixes: SIGSEGV with a non-array second argument to
                xhprof_enable(), with ignored_functions containing "main()",
                and with SQL callbacks; SIGFPE with
                xhprof.sampling_interval=0.
              - Robustness: reports no longer return HTTP 500 on malformed
                run data (non-numeric metric values are sanitized to 0,
                non-array entries dropped); division-by-zero guards added
                in callgraph generation.
              - Tests: add xhprof_014 ~ xhprof_018.
              - PHP 8.6 compatibility: builds cleanly and passes the full test
                suite against 8.6.0RC2 (no source changes required); PHP 8.5
                still builds and passes the same suite.
              - Behavior changes:
                (1). xhprof_enable() now throws a TypeError when the second
                     argument is not an array (previously a segmentation
                     fault).
                (2). More than 256 ignored_functions entries are truncated
                     with a warning.
                (3). The charset allowed for custom run ids/types is narrowed
                     to [A-Za-z0-9_.-].

